        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f46" parent="d1" value="Contact details" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;endArrow=classic;endFill=1;exitX=0;exitY=0.5000;entryX=1;entryY=0.2857;exitPerimeter=0;entryPerimeter=0;" edge="1" source="B_D1b" target="P10.0">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f47" parent="d1" value="Notification record" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;endArrow=classic;endFill=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.7143;entryX=0;entryY=0.5000;exitPerimeter=0;entryPerimeter=0;" edge="1" source="P10.0" target="B_D11">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="v0" parent="d1" value="Approved changes" edge="1" source="P9.0" target="P8.0" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;endArrow=classic;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;exitPerimeter=0;entryPerimeter=0;">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="v1" parent="d1" value="Content-update notices" edge="1" source="P8.0" target="P10.0" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;rounded=0;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;endArrow=classic;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;exitPerimeter=0;entryPerimeter=0;">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" parent="d1" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. The session / role token from 1.0 accompanies every request (not drawn).&lt;br&gt;2. 1.0 also writes login events to the audit log (not drawn). 3.0 and 9.0 also send reminder and alert requests to 10.0, and 8.0 sends content-update notices (the 3.0 and 9.0 requests are not drawn to keep lines straight). E5 delivers reminders to travellers and officers.&lt;br&gt;3. Checklist items in D2 carry the rule, version and requirement level used, so scores can be reproduced. No document numbers or uploads are stored.&lt;br&gt;4. AI suggestions (D9) never change published content until a second administrator approves them in 9.0; 8.0 publishes approved changes. E4 and E6 are the same external entities as in the Level 0 context diagram." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1986" width="1250" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram name="7 ERD as built (PostgreSQL)" id="erd-as-built">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1200" dy="800" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="1700" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="r0" />
        <mxCell id="r1" parent="r0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="r1" value="&lt;b&gt;ERD as built&lt;/b&gt; (exported from the PostgreSQL schema, migrations 001-004)" style="text;html=1;align=left;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="-50" width="1400" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend" parent="r1" value="PK = primary key, FK = foreign key. Rules are stored as JSON in &lt;b&gt;pt_admin_requirements.rule_metadata&lt;/b&gt; (nationality groups, purposes, travel mode, border post) instead of separate lookup tables. Roles use a join table (many roles per user). Officers can be assigned to several border posts. The QR table stores a SHA-256 digest of the signed token, never the token itself. Content and rules follow draft, pending review, approved, published." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="-15" width="1400" height="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
